  "historical_rows_closed": {
    "838": "Compared the complete Mirage class. Its resource callback is a static member paired with the existing teardown. The native constructor and factory use the concrete actor types. The material accumulator at 0x430 is NJS_ARGB and covers all four historical floats. The existing can_hit_same_target virtual slot and return type keep the upstream interface"
  },
  "historical_rows_with_added_evidence": {
    "456": "Formation removal takes the actual Canadin pointer in the existing virtual slot. The hover helpers are native members and the map-core reset takes the shared color record. The remaining historical actor declarations need source comparison",
    "589": "The native hover calls keep the original 0x8009EB14 and 0x8009EB98 methods. The leader removes the concrete member pointer, reorders the live member array and sets the thresholds as in retail. The color-reset callers pass their NJS_ARGB directly. Other historical source changes remain open",
    "727": "The move collision check takes a const destination vector and the three movement states are native nonvirtual methods. The existing action virtual and equal field names are retained. The remaining historical parameter and state structure changes need source comparison",
    "778": "The Mirage resource callback owns a copied Ginja texture list and keeps the original alternate-slot copy direction and NPC registration. Render saves and restores borrowed entry pointers using their real type. Other attack and movement changes remain open",
    "814": "The native factory, movement collision method and three movement-state methods keep the original addresses. The loader and renderer use typed Ginja texture entries, including the distinct alternate copy direction. Other historical changes remain open",
    "958": "The alternate texture-list allocation, copy, material swap and restoration use native Ginja types and the real copy provider. The remaining historical behavior needs source comparison"
  },
  "existing_upstream_interfaces_kept": {},
